WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.560
Well, I think just, you know, looking at racism squarely in the face for what it was, you know:

2
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:18.140
legions of fraternal organizations that didn’t accept blacks, a football team that had actually not had its first black football player by that time.

3
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.960
So I was to help usher in, truly, a new era here.

4
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:31.340
To this day, my best friend is the first recruit . . . first black recruit to the LSU football team.

5
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.580
That was well over twenty years ago, Lora Hinton.

6
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:40.800
So, I was there and I . . . One thing that I remember about the white kids is that they were open,

7
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:47.800
they were ready, that . . . That Lora walked around as a . . . some god, you know.

8
00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:56.180
I mean, and was just so socially advanced anyway that it was a piece of cake for him, really.

9
00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:03.440
Well, the history of LSU, ’69 was one of the best years that you could have come, as far as the environment on campus.

10
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:10.120
A lot of movement had taken place in ’68, so you walked into a little bit more openness in the environment.

11
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:10.540
Well, I did.
